  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 305 AM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nLight winds and mainly clear skies take hold Wednesday night and \nallow temperatures to drop an extra few degrees into the 40s to low \n50s. Daytime highs on Thursday and Friday sit near normal around 70F \nfor most locations. By late Friday, the next system moves into the \nregion and increases rain chances from west to east into the day on \nSaturday. Medium to long range guidance continues to show an upper \nlevel disturbance crossing northern Mexico and into southwest \nTexas on Saturday. Highest rain chances continue to be south of \nthe I-10 corridor. Areas to the north having markedly lower rain \nchances(10- 30% compared to 40-60%), but shifts in the track of \nthis low will affect which areas see the best chances and highest \namounts of rain. Beyond Saturday, the upper low moves out of the \narea and the forecast shifts drier with seasonable temperatures in\nthe 60 and 70s during the day with 40s and 50s at night. \n\n-Stickney",
